      "id": 100,
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## Tetragon \u2014 kernel-syscall security watch\n\nTetragon attaches BPF programs to **every interesting kernel hook**: `execve`, `clone`, `exit`, `security_file_open`, `tcp_connect`, capability checks, LSM hooks. The result is a stream of structured events with full kernel context (PID, parent PID, command-line, file path, capabilities, return code) for everything the kernel actually does.\n\nNo agent install, no app instrumentation, no log scraping \u2014 same data Falco produces but with first-class K8s pod attribution and lower overhead."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Process activity surface (every fork + exec + exit)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "id": 110,
